{"kind":"article","topicSections":[{"title":"SHAP Explainer APIs","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/KernelSHAP"],"anchor":"SHAP-Explainer-APIs"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SHAP (SHapley Additive exPlanations)"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" is a game-theoretic approach to explain the output of any machine learning model. It connects optimal credit allocation with local explanations using the classic Shapley values from cooperative game theory.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"1-The-Four-Shapley-Axioms","text":"1. The Four Shapley Axioms","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Shapley values are the only attribution method that uniquely satisfies all four fundamental properties:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Efficiency"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Feature attributions sum up to the difference between model prediction "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"f(x)"},{"type":"text","text":" and expected background prediction "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"E[f(X)]"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"name":"Note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Σ_i=1..M φ_i = f(x) - E[f(X)]"}]}],"style":"note"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Symmetry","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": If two features contribute equally to all possible feature subsets, their attributions are equal."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Dummy (Null Player)"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": A feature that does not change the model prediction for any coalition receives an attribution of zero (","type":"text"},{"code":"φ_i = 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Additivity"}]},{"text":": For ensemble models ","type":"text"},{"code":"f = f1 + f2","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", attributions satisfy "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"φ_i(f) = φ_i(f1) + φ_i(f2)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"text":"2. Explaining Predictions in SwiftSci","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"2-Explaining-Predictions-in-SwiftSci"},{"code":["import SwiftExplain","import SwiftML","","\/\/ Initialize KernelSHAP with background dataset","let explainer = try KernelSHAP(","    model: { features in","        \/\/ Arbitrary inference closure","        return try await rf.predictProba(features: features).map { $0[1] }","    },","    background: backgroundSamples,","    nSamples: 100",")","","\/\/ Compute Shapley values for an instance","let instance = [35.0, 75000.0, 720.0, 1.0]","let explanation = try await explainer.explain(instance: instance)","","print(\"Base Value: \\(explanation.baseValue)\")","print(\"Feature Attributions: \\(explanation.values)\")"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftexplain\/kernelshaptheory"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/KernelSHAPTheory","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Compute exact and sampled Shapley feature attributions to explain predictions of any machine learning model."}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"API Collection","title":"Game-Theoretic Interpretability with Kernel SHAP","modules":[{"name":"SwiftExplain"}],"role":"collectionGroup"},"references":{"doc://SwiftExplain/documentation/SwiftExplain":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain","abstract":[{"text":"Model Explainability, SHAP & Feature Attributions.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","type":"topic","title":"SwiftExplain","url":"\/documentation\/swiftexplain","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SwiftExplain/documentation/SwiftExplain/KernelSHAP":{"type":"topic","title":"KernelSHAP","url":"\/documentation\/swiftexplain\/kernelshap","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Model interpretation using the KernelSHAP algorithm.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"KernelSHAP"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/KernelSHAP","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"KernelSHAP"}]}}}